BUG 1 -- analyst notes were being scored as employer evidence   [FIXED, KEPT]
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
[2026-09-03 02:52] bug_found          The PSG / Sleep Tech listing scored 81/100 APPLY NOW with the
                                      reason "Trains you: abret". The word "abret" appears nowhere
                                      in that posting. It appeared only in a NOTE I had written
                                      speculating the role might be ABRET-adjacent.
                                      listing_text() was concatenating the notes field into the
                                      text used for keyword matching, so the board was reading its
                                      own commentary back as fact and promoting jobs on it.
                                      Same contamination inflated every RBT listing: my note
                                      "most ABA companies pay for the 40-hour RBT certification"
                                      became a matched training signal.
                                      Severity: high. This is the exact failure mode of a job board
                                      that confidently recommends the wrong thing.

[2026-09-03 02:55] test_written       test_notes_do_not_influence_score. Confirmed failing:
                                      bare=67.8 vs noted=89.6, a 21.8-point phantom lift.

[2026-09-03 02:58] fix_applied        Removed listing.get("notes") from listing_text(). Documented
                                      the reason in the docstring so it is not re-added.

[2026-09-03 02:58] fix_verified       61/61 tests pass. Phantom lift gone. Notes still render on the
                                      board for Stacey to read; they just cannot move the number.
                                      VERDICT: KEEP.

