BREAKTHROUGH -- LinkedIn is fully readable without a login
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
[2026-09-03 05:05] method_found      Stacey pasted a LinkedIn job search URL. Two endpoints turn out
                                     to work through WebFetch with no authentication at all:
                                       1. linkedin.com/jobs/view/<id>        -> full posting, full
                                          qualifications section, verbatim.
                                       2. linkedin.com/jobs/search?keywords=..&location=..&f_TPR=..
                                          -> enumerated 60 Florida neurodiagnostic postings WITH
                                          their numeric job IDs, which then feed endpoint 1.
                                     This is the complete LinkedIn pipeline. No scraper, no Composio,
                                     no MCP integration, no credentials. The earlier answer that
                                     LinkedIn needed a login was wrong for reading postings; it is
                                     only true for applying and for messaging.
                                     WORKFLOW FOR EVERY FUTURE SESSION: guest search to get IDs, then
                                     /jobs/view/<id> for the qualifications, then score.

